# Prettier ignore list.
#
# Vendored third-party copies are never formatted: they are not ours to reformat, they
# would produce unreviewable diffs, and at least one of them crashes the Prettier parser
# outright (`components/libs/social-media-embed/…/EmbedStyle.tsx`).
# See docs/harness/GOLDEN-RULES.md R7.

# --- vendored ------------------------------------------------------------------------
packages/pastebar-app-ui/src/components/libs/
src-tauri/libs/

# --- generated -----------------------------------------------------------------------
packages/pastebar-app-ui/dist-ui/
packages/pastebar-app-ui/tailwind-safelist.txt
tailwind-safelist.txt
packages/pastebar-app-ui/assets/markdown/markdown.js
packages/pastebar-app-ui/assets/styles/

# --- lockfiles (managed by npm, not by hand) -----------------------------------------
package-lock.json
packages/pastebar-app-ui/package-lock.json

# --- editor state (gitignored, so it must be ignored here too) -----------------------
# `.gitignore` excludes `.vscode/*` except `extensions.json`, but Prettier reads its own
# ignore file and walked straight into a developer's machine-generated settings.json. That
# file is not in the repository, yet it failed the format gate locally — a check that can
# be broken by something you did not write and cannot review is worse than no check.
.vscode/

# --- build/test output ---------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
target/
coverage/
*.timestamp-*.mjs

# --- translation resources (large generated YAML/JSON trees) -------------------------
packages/pastebar-app-ui/src/locales/lang/
packages/pastebar-app-ui/src/locales/date-locales/
src-tauri/src/services/translations/translations.yaml
